<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20362" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hĕlĭcon</span></b> ,
			ōnis, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑλικών</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a mountain in Bœotia</i>, <i>sacred to Apollo and the Muses</i>, now <i>Zagará</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 3, 4,
				§ 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4,
				7, 12, § 25</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 2,
				219</span></i>; <i><span class="en">5, 254</span></i>; <i><span class="en">663</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. F. 4,
				193</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 7, 641</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 163
			al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hĕlĭcōnĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Helicon</i>, <i>Heliconian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">collis,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Helicon</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					61, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tempe,</span>”
				<i>a beautiful valley on Mount Helicon</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Am. 1, 1, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mella,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. Laud. Ser. 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Naïs,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Epigr. 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hĕlĭcōnĭădes</span></b> ,
				um, f., <i>the
				Heliconians</i>, a <b>poet.</b> designation of
				<i>the Muses</i>, <i><span class="en">Lucr. 3,
				1037</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hĕlĭcōnis</span></b> ,
			ĭdis. f.
			adj., <i>Heliconian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">silva,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 4, 4, 90</span></i>
			.—In <i>plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hĕlĭcōnĭdes</span></b> ,
				 um, i. q. Heliconiades, <i>the
			Muses</i>, Pers. prooem. 4.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
